## Data Flow Through Layers

### Single Layer Processing

```
Cycle 0-1:   [LOAD_WEIGHTS]
             • Load input from previous layer (or initial input)
             • Load weights for current layer
             • Prepare systolic array inputs

Cycle 2:     [START_MATMUL]
             • Assert systolic_start signal
             • Begin matrix multiplication

Cycle 3-12:  [WAIT_MATMUL]
             • Systolic array processes data
             • Data flows through PE array
             • Accumulation occurs at each PE

Cycle 13:    [APPLY_BIAS]
             • VPU operation = BIAS_ADD
             • Add bias_layer[N] to all 9 outputs

Cycle 14-15: [APPLY_ACTIVATION]
             • VPU operation = activation function
             • Apply ReLU, Sigmoid, etc.
             • Wait for VPU to complete

Cycle 16-17: [STORE_RESULT]
             • Store processed output to layer buffer
             • Prepare for next layer

Cycle 18:    [NEXT_LAYER]
             • Increment layer counter
             • Check if more layers remain
             • If yes → back to LOAD_WEIGHTS
             • If no → COMPLETE
```

### Multi-Layer Execution Timeline

```
Time (cycles) →

0─────10────20────30────40────50────60

Layer 0:  [L][MatMul──][B][A][S]
                              └─→ Layer 1: [L][MatMul──][B][A][S]
                                                              └─→ Layer 2: [L][MatMul──][B][A][S]
                                                                                              └─→[DONE]

Legend:
[L] = Load Weights
[MatMul] = Matrix Multiplication (~10 cycles)
[B] = Apply Bias
[A] = Apply Activation
[S] = Store Result
```

