## Memory Organization

### Layer Buffer
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│      LAYER BUFFER (9 × 32-bit)      │
│                                     │
│  [0][1][2][3][4][5][6][7][8]        │
│                                     │
│  Stores:                            │
│  • Initial input (first layer)      │
│  • Intermediate results             │
│  • Input for next layer             │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Configuration Storage
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│    PER-LAYER CONFIGURATION ARRAYS        │
│                                          │
│  bias_layer[0:NUM_LAYERS-1]              │
│  [10][5][0]  (example for 3 layers)      │
│                                          │
│  vpu_ops_layer[0:NUM_LAYERS-1]           │
│  [ReLU][ReLU][Sigmoid]                   │
│                                          │
│  scale_layer[0:NUM_LAYERS-1]             │
│  [256][256][256]  (1.0 in fixed-point)   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Weight Memory (External)
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│        WEIGHT STORAGE                    │
│                                          │
│  Layer 0 Weights: [W00...W08] (9 vals)   │
│  Layer 1 Weights: [W00...W08] (9 vals)   │
│  Layer 2 Weights: [W00...W08] (9 vals)   │
│                                          │
│  Accessed via:                           │
│  weights[0:8] ← load(current_layer)      │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

